gap> LoadPackage("gapcxx");
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Loading gapcxx 0.1 (A C++ kernel extension providing secure, bidirectional memory converters between GAP objects and native C++ data structures.)
by Juan David Ferreira (https://gitlab.com/juniors90/).
Homepage: https://juniors90.github.io/gapcxx/
Report issues at https://github.com/juniors90/gapcxx/issues
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
true
gap> allT               := List(CXX_data_tensor_int, r -> r.1_tensor_2);;
gap> allS               := List( CXX_mat_s_int, r -> r.(Position(CXX_mat_s, r)) );;
gap> t0 := NanosecondsSinceEpoch();;
gap> parallel_results   := TestDimHomAllIntegerParallel(allT, allS);;
gap> # ================================
gap> #   Fin del código principal
gap> # ================================
gap> t1 := NanosecondsSinceEpoch();;
gap> # Calcular duración en segundos
gap> dur := (t1 - t0) / 1000000000.0;;
gap> # Convertir a horas, minutos y segundos
gap> horas := Int(dur / 3600);;
gap> minutos := Int((dur - horas * 3600) / 60);;
gap> segundos := Round(dur - horas * 3600 - minutos * 60);;
gap> # Mostrar resultado
gap> Print("\n=====================================\n");

=====================================
gap> Print("Tiempo total de ejecución:\n");
Tiempo total de ejecución:
gap> Print(String(horas), " horas, ", String(minutos), " minutos, ", String(segundos), " segundos.\n");
0 horas, 0 minutos, 8. segundos.
gap> Print("=====================================\n");
=====================================
gap> sequential_results := [];;
gap> t2 := NanosecondsSinceEpoch();;
gap> for t in allT do
>     for s in allS do
>         Add( sequential_results, CXX_DimHomAModules(t, s) );
>     od;
> od;
gap> # ================================
gap> #   Fin del código principal
gap> # ================================
gap> t3 := NanosecondsSinceEpoch();;
gap> # Calcular duración en segundos
gap> dur := (t3 - t2) / 1000000000.0;;
gap> # Convertir a horas, minutos y segundos
gap> horas := Int(dur / 3600);;
gap> minutos := Int((dur - horas * 3600) / 60);;
gap> segundos := Round(dur - horas * 3600 - minutos * 60);;
gap> # Mostrar resultado
gap> Print("\n=====================================\n");

=====================================
gap> Print("Tiempo total de ejecución:\n");
Tiempo total de ejecución:
gap> Print(String(horas), " horas, ", String(minutos), " minutos, ", String(segundos), " segundos.\n");
0 horas, 0 minutos, 34. segundos.
gap> Print("=====================================\n");
=====================================
gap> parallel_results = sequential_results;
true
gap> quit;
